		(uuid "6120ee05-14ca-51f5-a107-d347eddef906")
	)
	(text "Sidecar (U2) wiring: docs/sidecar_wiring.pdf. Link: LINK_TX (U1 GPIO0 -> U2 GPIO9), LINK_RX (U2 GPIO46 -> J3 pin 3), LINK_BCLK (U1 GPIO48 -> U2 GPIO10).\nJ3 selects U1 GPIO21 (U1_GPIO21, pin 2): jumper 1-2 = PBI RFSH (REFRESH), 2-3 = Sidecar link RX (LINK_RX).\nChanged from espBusBang: U1 GPIO0 no longer reaches the PBI bus; PBI AUDIO (J1.49) is driven by the Sidecar (U2 GPIO47, SC_AUDIO) through R7; U1 GPIO21 reaches RFSH only through J3; U1 GPIO48 left R1/RESET (RESET_DRV unconnected).\nU1 R/W regroup: GPIO15 = R/W (READ), GPIO16 = A14, GPIO17 = A15 (was A14, A15, R/W): needs the firmware changes in README.md.\nSerial flashing of U1 by U2 (Atari off): MAIN_EN (U2 GPIO11, open drain, to U1 EN), BOOT = LINK_TX (U2 GPIO9 to U1 IO0), SC_FLASH_TX (U2 GPIO12) -R12-> D6 = U1 RXD0, SC_FLASH_RX (U2 GPIO13) <-R13- D5 = U1 TXD0.\nJ8 RFSH -> U1 GPIO20, J9 RESET_DRV (R1) -> U1 GPIO19, J10 Sidecar 5V -> carrier 5V: all fitted = the sidecar_pcb_xl wiring (U1 USB unusable); J8/J9 open = U1 USB console as usual.\nD2: MPD_ activity LED (3V3 - R17 - D2 - MPD): lit while MPD_ is asserted (PBI ROM in use).\nU2 profiler inputs: PHI2, READ, EXTSEL, D0, D1, A0, REFRESH. J2: microSD breakout, 10k pull-ups R2-R6 to the Sidecar's own 3V3 (SC_3V3); U1 and U2 3V3 never tied."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 172.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "84c304a3-b947-583f-b3ba-0c226e599030")
	)
